# Develop-gate verification for pi-ensemble — AGENTS.md §1, mechanically.
#
# Without this file the resolver falls through to `npm run test`, which is three
# smoke tests out of ~120, no typecheck and no lint. The gate that is supposed
# to prove a developer's diff builds was proving almost nothing.
#
# The full §1 gate is `bun run build` too, but build writes into dist/ and this
# runs once per workstream worktree in parallel; the deeper suite lives in
# .pi/verify-cmd-full, which the ci step runs once.
#
# PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_TEST_JOBS is sized from the host here, not a new default:
# the pool in lib/verify-pool.sh ships 2, and while the suite alone finishes in
# 8m55s — inside the bound — the FULL command under load (the two typechecks,
# the lint, and the suite, with other /work cycles running) took ~19 min on this
# host at JOBS=2, which blows the binding bound: the develop gate's 10-min
# wall-clock, PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_MS (verifyTimeoutMs, #1324). The
# measurement covers the suite stage alone; the surrounding gates are what push
# it past 10 min.
#
# 4 jobs on a host with 8 or more CPUs, 2 otherwise — a small host gains nothing
# from a wide pool and pays for it in contention. An explicit ambient setting of
# the variable wins over the host-derived value. Measured on a 10-core host at
# the suite stage: JOBS=2 → 8m55s, JOBS=4 → 4m49s, same failures at both. JOBS=6
# and above made test-cancel.ts flaky, so the pool is not widened further.
#
# `--jobs-from-host` is how that sizing reaches the pool, and it lives in the
# script rather than as an inline `PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_TEST_JOBS="${…:-$(getconf
# …)}"` prefix because the review-accept guard (#1125) refuses any command word
# carrying a shell expansion — `$`, backtick, braces. On an agent-run command no
# flag ban separates a benign `${VAR:-$(…)}` from an injection, so the guard's
# A5 arm admits `bash smoke-tests/lib/verify-loop.sh <suites>` and nothing with
# an expansion in it. That rule is the guard's, not this file's, so the
# expansion moved behind a flag the script owns. The flag is opt-in and CI does
# not pass it, so .github/workflows/ci.yml keeps the shipped default of 2 — the
# same shape as before #1365, and the reason the host lookup is opt-in rather
# than the pool's own default. test-review-accept-guard-hardened.ts reads this
# file arm by arm and pins that every one of them passes the guard.
cd extension && bun x tsc --noEmit && bun x tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.smoke-tests.json && cd .. && bun run check && cd extension && bash smoke-tests/lib/verify-loop.sh --jobs-from-host smoke-tests/test-*.ts
